00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.410
Whiting, or Japanese whiting to be more precise.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:50.290
Their slender, pale, and
almost translucent appearance

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.700
gave them the nickname "Queen of the Sea."

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:57.080
Because they're whitefish and have no
fishy taste, they're excellent as tempura.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.700
Whiting live in the shallow part of the sea,

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:03.410
basically the surf zones on the beach.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:07.700
Oh, so like the Kamegahama
Seaside Park near our club room.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:10.750
Yup. You'll find them there.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.330
Young whiting are only about 20 cm long and swim

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.910
right near the beach on
the shallow end of the water.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:18.830
Ya just give the rod a li'l flick,
and it's EZ as pie.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:21.540
